    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d193">

                <pb facs="0362" n="248" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg248"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">354.116 M 81/1: Circular telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wright</hi>)<anchor n="30"
                        xml:id="d193-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-04-05T13:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 5, 1921—1
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Department advised that British diplomatic and consular officers here refuse
                    visas to American Mormon missionaries going to South Africa. Investigate and
                    report.</p>
                <p>Repeat <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis</hi> to The Hague, Copenhagen,
                    Christiania, and Berne.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d193-f1" n="30" type="source" xml:id="d193-f1-content">
                <p>See last paragraph for instructions to repeat to The Hague, Copenhagen,
                    Christiania, and Berne.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
